WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.339 --> 00:00:05.340
So most of the videos on Valuetainment are
directed to entrepreneurs, but today I want

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:11.170
to talk to the employees, who also follow
Valuetainment, but you're thinking about maybe

00:00:11.170 --> 00:00:15.220
one day becoming an entrepreneur, you just
don't know what to do next.

00:00:15.220 --> 00:00:20.690
Listen, there's 10 things I want you to be
doing, before thinking about entrepreneurship.

00:00:20.690 --> 00:00:26.560
I remember when I worked at Bally Total Fitness
and I had a job and it was comfortable.

00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:29.580
I had a salary and it was good for me.

00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:33.649
I wanted to become a business owner, I wanted
to become an entrepreneur, but there's a few

00:00:33.649 --> 00:00:36.230
things that I had to do before I made that
decision.

00:00:36.230 --> 00:00:37.680
I'm gonna cover with you here today.

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:42.390
By the way, I want you to know, it ain't for
everybody, so when I go through it, you may

00:00:42.390 --> 00:00:44.660
say, I can't do that, I can't do this.

00:00:44.660 --> 00:00:46.390
Well maybe it ain't for you.

00:00:46.390 --> 00:00:47.879
So let me get right into it here.

00:00:47.879 --> 00:00:48.879
10 things.

00:00:48.879 --> 00:00:49.879
Number one.

00:00:49.879 --> 00:00:50.879
You gotta learn how to self-motivate.

00:00:50.879 --> 00:00:55.030
I get too many messages man, that people tell
me, how do you motivate yourself.

00:00:55.030 --> 00:01:00.539
Can you, actually I get Snapchat messages,
Mario, people send me messages saying, "Pat,

00:01:00.539 --> 00:01:04.790
can you give me a motivational content for
me to get motivated?"

00:01:04.790 --> 00:01:09.130
If you don't know how to self-motivate yourself,
cross this thing out.

00:01:09.130 --> 00:01:15.609
If you do not know how to self motivate yourself
and get yourself fired up like this, business

00:01:15.609 --> 00:01:16.959
isn't for you.

00:01:16.959 --> 00:01:18.869
Because in a world of business you're alone.

00:01:18.869 --> 00:01:20.609
There's not gonna be somebody telling you're
amazing.

00:01:20.609 --> 00:01:24.700
There's gonna be actually people on the complete
opposite side, saying how horrible you are,

00:01:24.700 --> 00:01:26.679
constantly finding your leaks.

00:01:26.679 --> 00:01:29.219
Think about it this way here, so this maybe
makes sense to you.

00:01:29.219 --> 00:01:33.189
Any athlete that first gets into the league,
everybody picks at him.

00:01:33.189 --> 00:01:36.100
He doesn't know how to play defense, he doesn't
know how to do this.

00:01:36.100 --> 00:01:41.079
It takes six, seven, eight years until they
maybe win a championship, then they get off

00:01:41.079 --> 00:01:42.079
their back.

00:01:42.079 --> 00:01:44.009
The same is becoming an entrepreneur.

00:01:44.009 --> 00:01:47.689
You gotta learn to keep yourself up, you gotta
learn how to play hurt, you gotta learn how

00:01:47.689 --> 00:01:50.489
to stay motivated and get your people motivated.

00:01:50.489 --> 00:01:53.609
So you gotta learn how to self-motivate before
you become an entrepreneur.

00:01:53.609 --> 00:01:54.609
Number two.

00:01:54.609 --> 00:01:56.880
Save, save, save.

00:01:56.880 --> 00:01:58.020
Save your money.

00:01:58.020 --> 00:02:01.079
I saved my money when I worked at Bally's.

00:02:01.079 --> 00:02:03.840
I was working at Bally's but I was saving
that money.

00:02:03.840 --> 00:02:08.369
I was setting aside the money, because I knew
longterm, I was gonna be in sales.

00:02:08.369 --> 00:02:12.230
I didn't know what I was gonna sell and I
didn't know if I was gonna stay as an employee

00:02:12.230 --> 00:02:15.400
forever, because I wanted to figure out a
way to make more money.

00:02:15.400 --> 00:02:20.659
I did know sales was it, but I did know that
I needed my money in case if I went fully

00:02:20.659 --> 00:02:22.690
commission, what am I gonna do if I go fully
commission?

00:02:22.690 --> 00:02:23.690
Save, save, save.

00:02:23.690 --> 00:02:24.690
Number three.

00:02:24.690 --> 00:02:26.340
Learn how to sell.

00:02:26.340 --> 00:02:27.810
Today we had an entrepreneur that came here.

00:02:27.810 --> 00:02:31.960
He may be in the next vlog, I don't know Paul
if you're gonna put him on there or not, we'll

00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:32.960
figure it out.

00:02:32.960 --> 00:02:34.569
But he came today.

00:02:34.569 --> 00:02:43.209
His idea was, he has an app that he's designing
that's for what, that's for house cleaning.

00:02:43.209 --> 00:02:44.920
For instance, I'm in Houston.

00:02:44.920 --> 00:02:48.750
I want to a house cleaner to come to my house
tomorrow to clean it up.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:52.840
I get on there, I book them four hours, my
house is 2000 square feet, the pricing is

00:02:52.840 --> 00:02:54.750
gonna be $120.

00:02:54.750 --> 00:02:56.170
Somebody comes to my house.

00:02:56.170 --> 00:02:57.390
That's what he's designing.

00:02:57.390 --> 00:03:01.920
He comes here, Mario invites him to come to
the office, he's flabbergasted.

00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:05.230
He's got five to 10 minutes with us, and he
speaks for 10 minutes.

00:03:05.230 --> 00:03:06.230
You know what I asked him?

00:03:06.230 --> 00:03:08.590
I asked him the following question, "Do you
know how to sell?"

00:03:08.590 --> 00:03:09.590
He says, "I do."

00:03:09.590 --> 00:03:10.739
I said, "I'm telling you, you don't know how
to sell?"

00:03:10.739 --> 00:03:11.739
He says, "What do you mean?"

00:03:11.739 --> 00:03:15.060
I said, "10 minutes you're here, you haven't
asked a single question yet.

00:03:15.060 --> 00:03:18.230
You're just talking, talking, talking, talking,
talking, talking, talking, talking.

00:03:18.230 --> 00:03:20.689
So your business is not gonna work if you
don't know how to sell, you gotta learn how

00:03:20.689 --> 00:03:22.079
to sell.

00:03:22.079 --> 00:03:24.420
As an entrepreneur, if you're an employee
right, now you're working wherever you're

00:03:24.420 --> 00:03:25.420
working at.

00:03:25.420 --> 00:03:27.060
If you don't learn how to sell, what do you
think happens?

00:03:27.060 --> 00:03:29.299
All of a sudden you become an entrepreneur,
you don't know how to sell.

00:03:29.299 --> 00:03:31.250
You gotta learn how to sell.

00:03:31.250 --> 00:03:35.680
Before you make that plunge of becoming an
entrepreneur full-time, learn how to sell.

00:03:35.680 --> 00:03:38.930
Number four.

00:03:38.930 --> 00:03:41.200
Work for one, yeah, work for one.

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:43.379
Work under an entrepreneur.

00:03:43.379 --> 00:03:48.790
Work closely with a CEO, shadow one, see what
they do, see what's different about them.

00:03:48.790 --> 00:03:53.200
I'm talking about one that, today an entrepreneur,
I hear a lot of people that say, "You know,

00:03:53.200 --> 00:03:59.569
I work for a 72 year old very successful entrepreneur
who made a lot of his money, but he golfs

00:03:59.569 --> 00:04:01.139
every day."

00:04:01.139 --> 00:04:03.170
That's not who you want to work with.

00:04:03.170 --> 00:04:08.530
You want to work with the entrepreneur that
is starving, but he's on his way up so you

00:04:08.530 --> 00:04:09.849
can learn from him.

00:04:09.849 --> 00:04:12.499
I remember one time a guy called me, his name
was Brian.

00:04:12.499 --> 00:04:14.249
It was six o'clock in the morning.

00:04:14.249 --> 00:04:15.249
I pick up the call.

00:04:15.249 --> 00:04:20.420
He says, "I have a shot at working with this
guy, with this guy and this guy.

00:04:20.420 --> 00:04:21.769
Who do you think I should be working with?"

00:04:21.769 --> 00:04:22.769
You know what I told him?

00:04:22.769 --> 00:04:23.910
I said, "Me."

00:04:23.910 --> 00:04:26.390
He said, "Come on Patrick, why you?"

00:04:26.390 --> 00:04:27.390
I said, "100% me."

00:04:27.390 --> 00:04:29.900
He says, "Tell me why."

00:04:29.900 --> 00:04:33.920
I said, "Do you want to work with somebody
that tells you stories on what they used to

00:04:33.920 --> 00:04:35.319
do when they worked 20 years ago.

00:04:35.319 --> 00:04:38.130
Or do you want to work with somebody that's
doing it today?

00:04:38.130 --> 00:04:40.950
They're working 80-100 hours a week, because
they're in the hunt.

00:04:40.950 --> 00:04:41.950
If they don't, they're gonna be out of business.

00:04:41.950 --> 00:04:43.280
I'm that guy.

00:04:43.280 --> 00:04:44.800
You should be working directly with me."

00:04:44.800 --> 00:04:47.650
A week later, we had a meeting at P.F.

00:04:47.650 --> 00:04:49.520
Chang's, they started working with us.

00:04:49.520 --> 00:04:50.520
Why?

00:04:50.520 --> 00:04:51.520
Because that's how you learn the most.

00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:52.860
Number five.

00:04:52.860 --> 00:04:59.690
Network, build contacts, relationships, whatever
you're doing, everything to you is just relationship,

00:04:59.690 --> 00:05:02.539
relationship, relationship, relationship,
relationship.

00:05:02.539 --> 00:05:06.580
We just had a call right now with a guy, that
will also be on the vlog, I just got back

00:05:06.580 --> 00:05:09.919
from [inaudible 00:05:07], I was at [inaudible
00:05:07], I did and AIG event.

00:05:09.919 --> 00:05:11.650
This past week, that was a very big event.

00:05:11.650 --> 00:05:15.370
AIG just got a just got a new CEO, and a lot
of other things that we had to have a meeting

00:05:15.370 --> 00:05:16.810
with over there.

00:05:16.810 --> 00:05:20.590
When I came back, he's talking about, he wants
to invest, it's a big number that he wants

00:05:20.590 --> 00:05:21.590
to invest.

00:05:21.590 --> 00:05:24.640
We're not talking $5,000,000, we're talking
a lot of money that they want to invest.

00:05:24.640 --> 00:05:27.340
We're having this conversation together.

00:05:27.340 --> 00:05:32.680
And as we're having a conversation together,
Tom and I start talking, this whole thing,

00:05:32.680 --> 00:05:38.670
relationship came from 15 different contacts,
led to this.

00:05:38.670 --> 00:05:39.690
Okay?

00:05:39.690 --> 00:05:44.000
So network, build contacts, you never know
who is gonna introduce you to, people send

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:47.720
me a message and they say, "How do I find
an investor, Patrick, how?"

00:05:47.720 --> 00:05:50.320
What do you mean how do you find an investor?

00:05:50.320 --> 00:05:54.479
If you're a rookie entrepreneur, make a list
of everybody you know today.

00:05:54.479 --> 00:05:55.479
Then spread them out.

00:05:55.479 --> 00:05:57.349
By the way, that could be a whole different
episode.

00:05:57.349 --> 00:05:58.349
Spread them out.

00:05:58.349 --> 00:06:04.080
Who knows who, who knows who, who knows who,
who knows who, and then from there, contacts.

00:06:04.080 --> 00:06:07.300
As you're starting, as an employee you want
to become an entrepreneur.

00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:10.879
That [inaudible 00:06:07], that decision you
want to make, make a lot of, build a lot of

00:06:10.879 --> 00:06:11.879
contacts.

00:06:11.879 --> 00:06:12.879
Number six.

00:06:12.879 --> 00:06:16.409
Work 80 hours a week for 12 to 24 months and
see if you can do it or not.

00:06:16.409 --> 00:06:23.370
While I worked at Bally's, I worked 80 hours
every single week as an employee, and they

00:06:23.370 --> 00:06:29.199
only paid me four, you know, six dollars an
hour or seven dollars an hour, five dollars

00:06:29.199 --> 00:06:31.680
an hour, whatever the number was, because
it was commissions.

00:06:31.680 --> 00:06:34.870
But I worked 80, 90 hours per week.

00:06:34.870 --> 00:06:37.430
I was at the gym from morning until night.

00:06:37.430 --> 00:06:38.910
Every day I was at the gym.

00:06:38.910 --> 00:06:39.910
You know why?

00:06:39.910 --> 00:06:43.550
Because I wanted to see if I had what it takes
to work.

00:06:43.550 --> 00:06:48.960
Because if you don't know how to work 80 hours
a week as an employee, you are definitely

00:06:48.960 --> 00:06:50.449
not gonna be making it as an entrepreneur.

00:06:50.449 --> 00:06:54.629
If you go full time and you want to make a
business, you're gonna be required to work

00:06:54.629 --> 00:06:55.629
regularly.

00:06:55.629 --> 00:06:59.470
I think a lot of times people have this idea
that you become an entrepreneur, because when

00:06:59.470 --> 00:07:01.669
you become an entrepreneur, you're gonna become
a millionaire.

00:07:01.669 --> 00:07:02.759
[inaudible 00:07:02].

00:07:02.759 --> 00:07:03.759
Don't get me wrong.

00:07:03.759 --> 00:07:05.080
That eventually happens.

00:07:05.080 --> 00:07:07.919
It took me a few years and then it happens
and you have the money and the lifestyle,

00:07:07.919 --> 00:07:09.789
all this other stuff.

00:07:09.789 --> 00:07:16.419
But you going to become an entrepreneur to
create something and there's a risk that constantly,

00:07:16.419 --> 00:07:19.389
that's being taken to want to grow the business.

00:07:19.389 --> 00:07:23.389
So if you don't know how to work hard and
you lose your edge, boom, somebody comes and

00:07:23.389 --> 00:07:25.900
takes the market away from you, because you
lost your edge.

00:07:25.900 --> 00:07:29.370
So if you don't know if you have it, you're
right now working nine to five, why don't

00:07:29.370 --> 00:07:32.570
you work 80 hours a week at your job and see
what happens?

00:07:32.570 --> 00:07:34.410
I'm dead serious with you.

00:07:34.410 --> 00:07:38.130
First of all, you may get some crazy promotions
out of nowhere.

00:07:38.130 --> 00:07:42.509
You may be there and having real, direct,
private conversations with the CEO, because

00:07:42.509 --> 00:07:44.960
the CEO is there, and you have him like, "My
gosh."

00:07:44.960 --> 00:07:46.879
CEO sees me every night, I leave after him.

00:07:46.879 --> 00:07:48.180
I come before him.

00:07:48.180 --> 00:07:49.180
What the hell is going on?

00:07:49.180 --> 00:07:51.420
Who is this guy, why is this guy working so
hard?

00:07:51.420 --> 00:07:56.610
Work 80 hours a week for 12 to 24 months to
see if you got it or not.

00:07:56.610 --> 00:07:57.610
Next.

00:07:57.610 --> 00:07:58.610
Research.

00:07:58.610 --> 00:08:01.229
Learn how to research and learn fast.

00:08:01.229 --> 00:08:02.229
Learn how to research.

00:08:02.229 --> 00:08:05.080
I think this thing about researching.

00:08:05.080 --> 00:08:10.050
Again, that's a whole different thing that
people, we can probably do one, how to research

00:08:10.050 --> 00:08:11.780
something, that could be an episode.

00:08:11.780 --> 00:08:15.319
I think researching is a skill.

00:08:15.319 --> 00:08:18.350
You gotta research who is this connected to,
who does this guy know, what's this thing

00:08:18.350 --> 00:08:21.139
all about, what is this product all about,
what is this guy, why did they come out with

00:08:21.139 --> 00:08:24.150
us, why did this happen, what does this law
have to do with this.

00:08:24.150 --> 00:08:26.080
You gotta learn how to research, okay.

00:08:26.080 --> 00:08:28.970
And you get to the bottom of something like,
this guy is connected to this guy.

00:08:28.970 --> 00:08:30.960
Now I get why this guy is saying this.

00:08:30.960 --> 00:08:32.780
Oh, this is starting to make sense.

00:08:32.780 --> 00:08:35.210
You get the click, I figured out what's going
on.

00:08:35.210 --> 00:08:37.510
I gotta learn how to research and learn fast.

00:08:37.510 --> 00:08:38.830
Number eight.

00:08:38.830 --> 00:08:39.830
Build an audience.

00:08:39.830 --> 00:08:42.440
Back in the days in 1990, when I worked at
Bally's, there was no Facebook.

00:08:42.440 --> 00:08:43.440
I think Facebook.

00:08:43.440 --> 00:08:48.170
I think Facebook was, Paul was Facebook 03
or 04, I want to say February of 04, is when

00:08:48.170 --> 00:08:49.460
I want to say Facebook was.

00:08:49.460 --> 00:08:50.610
There was nothing.

00:08:50.610 --> 00:08:56.640
Myspace I think was 01, 02, I don't know when
Myspace was, but there was nothing at Bally.

00:08:56.640 --> 00:08:58.790
There was no way to build an audience.

00:08:58.790 --> 00:09:02.020
But the way I built an audience, I built it
with everybody that was a member at the gym.

00:09:02.020 --> 00:09:04.940
I built an audience that worked at different
Bally's.

00:09:04.940 --> 00:09:06.460
I built a relationship there.

00:09:06.460 --> 00:09:07.650
But build an audience.

00:09:07.650 --> 00:09:08.970
Build an audience on social media.

00:09:08.970 --> 00:09:13.070
Build an audience on Snap, on Facebook, on
Instagram, on YouTube, on Twitter.

00:09:13.070 --> 00:09:15.150
Figure out a way to build an audience with
your voice.

00:09:15.150 --> 00:09:17.910
Number nine.

00:09:17.910 --> 00:09:22.890
As you're going through this and you're making
a decision to go here, start becoming self

00:09:22.890 --> 00:09:27.140
aware and aligned about what your own strengths
and weaknesses are.

00:09:27.140 --> 00:09:28.180
Figure that part out.

00:09:28.180 --> 00:09:33.970
[inaudible 00:09:29] You know what, I never
knew I was gonna be good in sales until I

00:09:33.970 --> 00:09:34.970
started working at Bally's.

00:09:34.970 --> 00:09:38.200
I mean, I used to sell at 10 years old.

00:09:38.200 --> 00:09:42.940
But I really started realizing, I can be pretty
good at this sales thing.

00:09:42.940 --> 00:09:45.730
Then I started realizing pressure.

00:09:45.730 --> 00:09:46.730
What happens in pressure.

00:09:46.730 --> 00:09:47.730
You know, deadlines.

00:09:47.730 --> 00:09:51.800
When we have numbers we have to hit, in sales,
we had closeouts on Thursdays.

00:09:51.800 --> 00:09:53.520
I'm okay with this.

00:09:53.520 --> 00:09:55.550
There was another guy, one of my managers
that I work with.

00:09:55.550 --> 00:10:00.400
He was my boss, he couldn't hack it himself,
but he was my boss.

00:10:00.400 --> 00:10:04.940
Great guy, a sweetheart, one thing I'll never
forget about him.

00:10:04.940 --> 00:10:07.060
He always told me, he says, "Pat, you curse
too much."

00:10:07.060 --> 00:10:09.700
Because I had just gotten out of the army
so every other word out of my mouth was a

00:10:09.700 --> 00:10:10.700
curse word.

00:10:10.700 --> 00:10:12.260
You see, you gotta slow this thing down.

00:10:12.260 --> 00:10:16.010
I'd be selling and cursing non-stop, so he
would always work with me on that.

00:10:16.010 --> 00:10:18.280
But I remember it was Thursday closeouts.

00:10:18.280 --> 00:10:20.260
We haven't hit our numbers yet.

00:10:20.260 --> 00:10:22.180
He would be panicking.

00:10:22.180 --> 00:10:26.380
There's a guy named Tony Willson, would call
in and no one wanted to pick up Tony's call,

00:10:26.380 --> 00:10:27.440
but I would pick up the call.

00:10:27.440 --> 00:10:29.510
"Tony, what's going on, why are you bothering
us?

00:10:29.510 --> 00:10:33.750
It's not done yet, let me finish up my day,
can I call you back at midnight?"

00:10:33.750 --> 00:10:34.750
"Yes."

00:10:34.750 --> 00:10:36.030
Didn't want to answer the phone call.

00:10:36.030 --> 00:10:38.660
Then boom, we would get two, three sales.

00:10:38.660 --> 00:10:39.660
How?

00:10:39.660 --> 00:10:43.200
I'd go on the walkway, I'd go in the gym,
I'd walk around, I would say, "Hey, how you

00:10:43.200 --> 00:10:44.200
doing, how is work?

00:10:44.200 --> 00:10:46.120
By the way, who do you know right now that's
looking for a membership?

00:10:46.120 --> 00:10:47.620
Why are you working out alone?

00:10:47.620 --> 00:10:51.140
Why don't you call your friends, let's get
them to become a member.

00:10:51.140 --> 00:10:52.730
Who can you call right now who can come to
the gym?

00:10:52.730 --> 00:10:53.950
Tell them to come to the gym."

00:10:53.950 --> 00:10:58.640
I would go through the members that are working
out and I would get them to call their friends

00:10:58.640 --> 00:11:02.330
to come to the gym and I'd sell them membership
that night, and boom, we would hit our numbers.

00:11:02.330 --> 00:11:03.330
Right?

00:11:03.330 --> 00:11:06.420
But it was, you kinda figuring out how to
make that part happen.

00:11:06.420 --> 00:11:08.180
So you learn your strengths and industries.

00:11:08.180 --> 00:11:10.850
I liked sales, I liked numbers.

00:11:10.850 --> 00:11:15.910
I started looking at which industries gave
a life, good life, I saw too many guys on

00:11:15.910 --> 00:11:19.390
real estate that were still selling in their
30th year and working on Sundays.

00:11:19.390 --> 00:11:22.380
I saw way too many guys in mortgages that
we're still selling.

